Source: pci-acs-scope
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: IriKa Qiu <qiujie.jq@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms, python3, git
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/ir1ka/pci-acs-scope
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/ir1ka/pci-acs-scope.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/ir1ka/pci-acs-scope

Package: pci-acs-scope-dkms
Architecture: all
Provides: pci-acs-scope (= ${binary:Version})
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 3.0), python3, kmod, xz-utils, zstd, gzip, coreutils, sed, grep, findutils, gawk | mawk
Recommends: linux-headers-amd64, pahole, initramfs-tools
Conflicts: pci-acs-scope-prebuilt, pci-acs-scope-native
Replaces: pci-acs-scope-prebuilt, pci-acs-scope-native
Description: opt-in ACS controls scoped to PCIe port subtrees
 Builds pci_acs_scope through DKMS without rebuilding the kernel.
 Only descendants of selected root/upstream/downstream ports change by default.
 Module loading is inert without execute=1 and a PCIe port list.
 Boot policy and read-only auditing require explicit enable commands.
 Installation never loads the module or enables a policy.

Package: pci-acs-scope-native
Architecture: all
Provides: pci-acs-scope (= ${binary:Version})
Pre-Depends: python3, zstd, lz4, lzop
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, grub2-common
Conflicts: pci-acs-scope-dkms, pci-acs-scope-prebuilt
Replaces: pci-acs-scope-dkms, pci-acs-scope-prebuilt
Description: explicit scoped ACS policy using native Linux PCI parameters
 Uses disable_acs_redir/config_acs and a dedicated GRUB drop-in.
 Pre-install checks every installed boot kernel for native support.
 No custom kernel module, DKMS registration or initramfs hook is shipped.
 Installation leaves policy disabled; user explicitly enables it.
